      "content": "i get that, but my doctor just tells me to drink more water and thats it, which is so frustrating. i read online that high doses of vitamin c are actually great for flushing out toxins and that the kidney stone thing is super rare if you stay hydrated. if i make sure i'm drinking like a gallon of water a day, wouldn't that pretty much cancel out the risk? i really want to go for the 3000mg dose to feel the benefits.",
